message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the following metadata."

title: "Fractal Literacy: Nature's Hidden Language"

type: article

authors:
  - family-names: "Alipour"
    given-names: "Dariush"

abstract: >
  This conceptual essay introduces fractal literacy as the ability
  to observe, recognize, interpret, and apply self-similar and
  multi-scale patterns in complex phenomena. It connects fractal
  patterns across nature, artificial intelligence, society, and
  philosophy, presenting fractal literacy as a conceptual bridge
  between these domains rather than as a report of new empirical
  findings.

keywords:
  - fractal geometry
  - fractal literacy
  - complexity
  - complex systems
  - artificial intelligence
  - neural networks
  - self-similarity
  - multi-scale patterns
  - social networks
  - philosophy of technology
  - Mandelbrot

